Package: hdstats
Type: Package
Title: High-Dimensional Penalized Huber, Quantile, and Rank Regression and Support Vector Machines
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-09-18
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Yikai", family = "Zhang", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "yikai-zhang@uiowa.edu"),
    person(given = "Qian", family = "Tang", role = "aut",
           email = "qian-tang@uiowa.edu"),
    person(given = "Boxiang", family = "Wang", role = "aut",
           email = "boxiang-wang@uiowa.edu"))
Description: Fits the entire regularization path of elastic-net penalized
    Huber regression, quantile regression, Wilcoxon rank regression, and
    linear support vector machines for high-dimensional data. The non-smooth
    hinge and check losses are handled by the finite smoothing algorithm of
    Tang, Zhang, and Wang (2024) <https://openreview.net/forum?id=RvwMTDYTOb>,
    which combines uniform-kernel convolution smoothing with coordinate
    descent, warm starts, and active-set or strong-rule screening. Nonconvex
    SCAD and MCP penalties are supported through the local linear
    approximation, and k-fold cross-validation with 'coef', 'predict',
    'print', and 'plot' methods is provided for tuning. The compute kernels
    are written in C++ via 'Rcpp'.
